# Anchored to the repository root on purpose. An unanchored `data/` matches a
# directory of that name at ANY depth, which silently swallowed the whole of
# src/arc/data/ -- the package was absent from every commit, so a fresh clone could
# not import arc.train.episodic at all. Same class of bug as the `--exclude data`
# in scripts/sync.sh (docs/HANDOFF.md section 6, landmine 11). Keep the slashes.
/data/
/logs/

# results/ is TRACKED on purpose, despite being generated output.
#
# ARC_SPEC section 8 makes "results are append-only" and "figures regenerate from
# results with one command" non-negotiable, and neither is enforceable if the results
# only exist on one un-backed-up machine. They were ignored until 2026-10-16, which
# meant every number in docs/ had exactly two copies: the compute box, which has no
# git repo of its own and is tar-synced, and whichever ephemeral cloud container last
# pulled them. Roughly 60 GPU-hours of measurements, one disk failure from gone.
#
# The whole tree is ~9 MB of JSON, which git compresses well, so there is no reason
# to be selective. New runs SHOULD show up as uncommitted work -- that is the
# append-only discipline being visible rather than assumed.
#
# Only genuinely reproducible-for-free artifacts stay out:
results/**/.done*
results/**/__pycache__/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
